 ones it's going  to be kind of just depends on what I  feel like and what turns out to be the  thing that works but um after this very  small-scale park I definitely am looking  for something bigger but I'm still quite  happy with maker Park even though it  didn't turn out to be as much of a  challenge as maybe  I had hoped for especially in the later  sections of the park the Dutch section  in particular I'm quite happy with how  it turned out try to really get that  cozy charming look to it and while there  is so many different things that I don't  like about this park which I'm try to  not go on about it was in the end also  really good learning experience  especially about the details that I  wanted to get in before I move on to  larger things again like L Fame and my  Christie Valley so yeah that is  basically what I wanted to say about  that  to get on the topic of this video a  little bit again most of the stuff which  I'm doing here is pretty much is filling  up the area so you could see I was  adding some lights in there some benches  I'm actually quite happy with how the  lights turn out even though they are  more or less a copy of the lights of the  eclectic Palace and a lot very open  foliage since this is a new area of the  park and especially these parts between  the paths and between the buildings kind  of I wanted to make them look as just  very newly planted areas where the  bushes still kind of need to grow and  where the trees are still very low I'm  not going to try and turn that into a  poem so yeah that's all just very simple  stuff but what I also wanted to do is  actually change the park border and you  can probably tell I'm trying to fit this  as much as I can within a rectangular  shape since part of what I wanted to do  with this park realism wise is actually  give it a real Park border and try and  stay within that and also have it have a  sort of realistic Park borders so it's  very square and it had to fit the park  in quite in a very 